#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:1
msgid "Source Installation on macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:3
msgid "This tutorial will work for macOS BigSur 10.16 and macOS Monterey 12.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:5
msgid "Install tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:7
msgid ""
"The use of some additional tools is recommended to help with the source "
"compilation, although other ways of correctly getting and building the "
"sources are also possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:10
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get the sources of all libraries is to use [vcstool]"
"(https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:13
msgid ""
"To compile all the different libraries and gz-sim in the right order [colcon]"
"(https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/) is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:16
msgid ""
"Tools and dependencies for Harmonic can be installed using the [Homebrew "
"package manager](https://brew.sh/). After installing Homebrew, add the `osrf/"
"simulation` to Homebrew tap to be able to install prebuilt dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:18
msgid ""
"brew tap osrf/simulation\n"
"brew trust osrf/simulation\n"
"brew update\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:24
msgid "Install compiler requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:26
msgid ""
"Building Gazebo Libraries require at least Xcode 10 on MacOS Mojave. The "
"Xcode Command Line Tools are sufficient, and can be installed with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:28
msgid "xcode-select --install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:32
msgid "Python 3 from Homebrew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:34
msgid ""
"Harmonic is compatible with Python 3. Install the latest version from "
"Homebrew:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:36
msgid "brew install python3\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:40
msgid "vcstool and colcon from PyPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:42
msgid "python3 -m pip install -U colcon-common-extensions vcstool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:46
msgid "Getting the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:48
msgid ""
"The first step is to create a developer workspace in which `vcstool` and "
"`colcon` can work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:51
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/workspace/src\n"
"cd ~/workspace/src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:56
msgid ""
"Use `vcstool` to automatically retrieve all the Gazebo libraries sources "
"from their repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:59
msgid ""
"vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gazebo-tooling/"
"gazebodistro/master/collection-harmonic.yaml src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:63
msgid "The src subdirectory should contain all the sources ready to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:65
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:67
msgid "Dependency for Ogre:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:69
msgid "brew install --cask xquartz\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:73
msgid "General dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:75
msgid ""
"brew install assimp boost bullet cmake cppzmq dartsim doxygen eigen fcl "
"ffmpeg flann freeimage freetype gdal gflags google-benchmark gts ipopt "
"jsoncpp libccd libyaml libzzip libzip nlopt ode open-scene-graph ossp-uuid "
"ogre1.9 ogre2.3 pkg-config protobuf qt@5 qwt-qt5 rapidjson ruby tbb tinyxml "
"tinyxml2 urdfdom zeromq\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:79
msgid ""
"`qt@5` is a \"keg only\" Homebrew formula and its path must be explicitly "
"configured before building Gazebo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:81
msgid ""
"# qt@5\n"
"export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=${CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:+$CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:}`brew --"
"prefix qt@5`\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:86
msgid "Unlink `qt` to avoid conflicts with other versions of qt (e.g. qt6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:88
msgid "brew unlink qt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:92
msgid "Building the Gazebo Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:94
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by changing into the workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:98
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
"colcon graph\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:103
msgid ""
"`colcon graph` should list the Gazebo libraries with an [interdependency "
"diagram](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/graph."
"html#example-output). If that is the case, then you are ready to build the "
"whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:108
msgid "colcon build --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:112
msgid ""
"Note if you are on an ARM based Apple Silicon Mac machine, you may need to "
"set a couple more cmake args:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:114
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args -DCMAKE_MACOSX_RPATH=FALSE -"
"DCMAKE_INSTALL_NAME_DIR=$(pwd)/install/lib --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:118
msgid "To speed up the build process, you could also disable tests by using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:120
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:124
msgid ""
"To use debuggers activate debug symbols. Gazebo will run slower, but you'll "
"be able to use `lldb`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:126
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args ' -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF' ' -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug' "
"--merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:130
msgid "To build a specific package with all its dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:132
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-up-to PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:136
msgid "To build a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:138
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-select PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:142
msgid ""
"Visit [colcon documentation](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/#) to "
"view more `colcon` build and test options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:144
msgid "If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:146
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:148
msgid "The workspace needs to be sourced every time a new terminal is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:150
msgid ""
"Run the following command to source the workspace in zsh (the default macOS "
"shell):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:152
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.zsh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:156
msgid "Or if you are using bash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:158
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.bash\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:162
msgid "You should now be able to launch gazebo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:164
msgid ""
"# launch server in one terminal\n"
"gz sim -v 4 shapes.sdf -s\n"
"\n"
"# launch gui in a separate terminal\n"
"# remember to source the workspace setup script\n"
"gz sim -v 4 -g\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:173
msgid ""
"This is the end of the source install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:176
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_osx_src.md:178
msgid "See [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md#macos)"
msgstr ""
